</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;TBARS (nmol/g)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">158.3 &#x000b1; 7.0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">166.6 &#x000b1; 12.4*</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;MDA + 4-HAE (nmol/g)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.1 &#x000b1; 1.5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.6 &#x000b1; 2.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;&#x003b1;-Tocopherol (nmol/g)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.9 &#x000b1; 4.0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.8 &#x000b1; 11.6*</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Abbreviations: ALDH, aldehyde dehydrogenase; GST, glutathione S-transferase; MDA + 4-HAE, malondialdehyde + 4-hydroxy-2-alkenal; TBARS, thiobarbituric acid-reactive substances.</p></fn><fn id="tblfn5"><label>1</label><p>Values are mean &#x000b1; SD, <italic>n</italic> = 6.</p></fn><fn><p>* Significant difference between the LA and DHA groups using Student&#x02019;s <italic>t</italic> test (<italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;3</label><caption><p>Major polyunsaturated fatty acid compositions of total lipids in the liver and kidney of ODS rats<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn6"><sup>1</sup></xref></p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Group</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">LA</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">DHA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1">g/100 g<hr/></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Liver</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02002;18:2 (<italic>n</italic>-6) LA<